<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the Friday to Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co Inc. Final numbers will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Romeo and Juliet ............ $11.6 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Sleepers ....................  $8.2 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) High School High ............. $5.1 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) Larger Than Life ............. $4.2 million</p>
<p>    5 (4) The Ghost and the Darkness ... $3.7 million</p>
<p>    6 (5) The First Wives Club ......... $3.62 million</p>
<p>    7 (3) Stephen King's Thinner ....... $3.6 million</p>
<p>    8 (*) Dear God ..................... $3.2 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) The Associate ................ $3.2 million</p>
<p>   10 (7) The Long Kiss Goodnight ...... $2.8 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;Sleepers&quot; is released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros. &quot;High School High&quot; is released by Sony Corp's TriStar Pictures. &quot;Larger Than Life&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by financier Kirk Kerkorian and Seven Network Ltd. &quot;The Ghost and the Darkness&quot;, &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; &quot;Stephen King's Thinner&quot; and &quot;Dear God&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;The Associate&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;The Long Kiss Goodnight&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner's Turner Broadcasting System.</p>
